  "title": "Ideas and biases stand in for copying genes",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "a80878cf-7e91-44ba-b305-e243963a7ade",
      "text": "Nature gives no way to copy a useful gene directly, which would speed up evolution. It gives ideas and biases instead: a useful idea can be copied, and even a fatal idea teaches others what not to do.",
